    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook reports a **clustering ablation** for the daily-brief LR ranker.\n",
        "\n",
        "### The question\n",
        "\n",
        "The LR engine builds cluster medoids (via Ward agglomerative clustering in `ranker/interests.js`, `buildInterests()`) from two inputs:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Input | Weight | Role |\n",
        "|-------|--------|------|\n",
        "| Perfect samples (`perfect_samples.json`) | `kappa` = 5 | Anchor the clusters |\n",
        "| Liked / saved items | 1 | Pull medoids toward recently-liked content |\n",
        "\n",
        "The **null hypothesis** is that liked items meaningfully shape the clusters and therefore the fitted model's AUC/logLoss. This ablation tests that by removing liked items from clustering (perfect samples only) and measuring the change in AUC/logLoss on a chronological holdout test set.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Experimental design\n",
        "\n",
        "Both conditions use the **exact same training rows, labels, and test split**; they differ **only** in which inputs seed the medoids:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Condition | Medoid inputs | Label |\n",
        "|-----------|--------------|-------|\n",
        "| `liked` | perfect samples (κ=5) **and** liked items (w=1) | Current behaviour |\n",
        "| `perfect` | perfect samples (κ=5) **only** | Ablation |\n",
        "\n",
        "Because the labels are identical, any AUC/logLoss difference is attributable to the medoids (which drive the `n:d1` distance-to-medoid numeric feature), not to different training data.\n",
        "\n",
        "The metric is computed via `node ranker/eval_clustering_ablation.js`, which wraps `ranker/pipeline.js` `evalModel()`: chronological holdout (80/20 by date), then prior / keyword (`rel`) / fitted Bayesian-LR AUC and logLoss on the test set.\n",
        "\n",
        "### How the experiment was run\n",
        "\n",
        "```bash\n",
        "python -m simulate.cli clustering-ablation --date 2026-11-01 --test-frac 0.2\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The Sacred experiment (`daily_brief_clustering_ablation`) invokes the Node.js helper once per condition, registers `config.json`, `perfect_samples.json`, `perfect-samples-new.json`, and `state.json` as resources, records `db_hash` as config, and persists the run to `docs/experiments/runs.db`.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Load latest Sacred run"
      ],
      "id": "17f6a22d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: load-latest-run\n",
        "def latest_clustering_ablation_run(db_path: str = str(RUNS_DB)) -> dict | None:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Fetch the most recent completed clustering-ablation Sacred run and parse its info JSON.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if not Path(db_path).exists():\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    con = sqlite3.connect(db_path)\n",
        "    con.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        rows = con.execute(\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "            SELECT r.id, e.name AS experiment, r.status, r.start_time, r.stop_time, r.info, r.result\n",
        "            FROM run r\n",
        "            JOIN experiment e ON e.experiment_id = r.experiment_id\n",
        "            WHERE e.name = 'daily_brief_clustering_ablation'\n",
        "              AND r.status = 'COMPLETED'\n",
        "            ORDER BY r.id DESC\n",
        "            LIMIT 1\n",
        "            \"\"\"\n",
        "        ).fetchall()\n",
        "    finally:\n",
        "        con.close()\n",
        "    if not rows:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    row = rows[0]\n",
        "    info = json.loads(row[\"info\"]) if row[\"info\"] else {}\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"run_id\": row[\"id\"],\n",
        "        \"status\": row[\"status\"],\n",
        "        \"start_time\": row[\"start_time\"],\n",
        "        \"stop_time\": row[\"stop_time\"],\n",
        "        \"info\": info,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "run = latest_clustering_ablation_run()\n",
        "if run is None:\n",
        "    print(\"No completed clustering-ablation run found in the Sacred DB.\")\n",
        "    print(\"Run: python -m simulate.cli clustering-ablation --date 2026-11-01 --test-frac 0.2\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    info = run[\"info\"]\n",
        "    print(f\"Run id: {run['run_id']}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Status: {run['status']}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Started: {run['start_time']}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Stopped: {run['stop_time']}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Date: {info.get('date')}, test_frac: {info.get('test_frac')}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"n_train: {info.get('n_train')}, n_test: {info.get('n_test')}, cutoff_date: {info.get('cutoff_date')}\")"
      ],
      "id": "load-latest-run",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
